    "title": "Stardom President Taro Okada Believes Stardom-NJPW Relationship Will Continue - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n1 hours ago\nAs previously reported, Bushiroad is transferring all shares in New Japan Pro-Wrestling (NJPW) to CyberAgent and TV Asahi , in a major move.\nThis comes 14 years after Bushiroad acquired NJPW in 2012, and Bushiroad has been the parent company of STARDOM since 2019.\nREAD MORE: Erick Stevens Stepping Away From Wrestling Yet Again\nREAD MORE: Updated Betting Odds For AAA Noche De Los Grandes\nSpeaking to Tokyo Sports , STARDOM President Taro Okada was hopeful that these changes wouldn’t prevent STARDOM from working with NJPW. He said,\n“We have a relationship where we lend and borrow wrestlers for special events and such, so we would like to continue doing various things together in the future, and I think it would be interesting to hold another joint event when the demand and timing are right.”\nA spokesperson for Bushroad added that the deal was made “to further strengthen cooperation in the development and rollout of content and IP, and to work together to create powerful content and IP with an eye toward global expansion, thereby further increasing the corporate value of both companies.”\nSTARDOM recently saw the return of one of its top names, two years after they left to join Marigold Wrestling. Click here to find out more.",
